# MirrorFit AI architecture rules

## Package boundaries

Dependencies flow in one direction. Do not introduce a cycle.

```
types  <-  validation  <-  protocol
types  <-  tryon-core
types  <-  ui
all packages  <-  apps/web
```

- `@mirrorfit/types` has no runtime dependencies. Domain vocabulary only.
- `@mirrorfit/validation` owns Zod primitives. Schemas derive from the const
  objects in `types` so a value cannot drift between layers.
- `@mirrorfit/protocol` owns the realtime wire format. It must not import
  Supabase. Business logic depends on `RealtimeTransport`, never on a concrete
  transport.
- `@mirrorfit/tryon-core` owns the vision pipeline interfaces. It must not
  import React or Next.

## Security invariants

These are not preferences.

- Never trust a client-supplied `organization_id`, `shop_id`, `display_id`,
  `role` or permission. Resolve tenancy server-side from the authenticated
  principal.
- The service role key appears only in modules that import `server-only`.
- Every value crossing a trust boundary is parsed with Zod, not cast.
- Pairing tokens are random, short-lived, single-use, revocable, and stored
  only as a keyed hash.
- Error responses returned to a customer device carry a coarse code and no
  diagnostic detail.

## Computer vision honesty

- Pose landmarks plus a PNG overlay is not photorealistic try-on. Do not
  describe it as such.
- A stage that is not implemented is marked `TODO`, `PLACEHOLDER` or
  `NOT PRODUCTION READY`. Do not ship a stub that reads as complete.
- Performance figures come from recorded samples via `MetricsCollector`.
  Never publish an estimated or hard-coded metric.
- A metric with no samples reports `null`, not `0`.

## Privacy

- Raw camera frames stay on the mirror. Do not add an upload path to the
  realtime loop.
- Any image leaving the device requires an explicit, purpose-specific,
  user-triggered consent record.
- Do not infer ethnicity, race, religion, medical conditions or any other
  sensitive attribute. Visual analysis is limited to product-matching signals.
- Recommendations are phrased as suggestions, never as objective truth.
